**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.PlanViewTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`

**How to implement.** The Plan view's ranked candidates, each with 'Add to kit' (001 §O 'Plan view: … and the ranked candidates, with "Add to kit"'; the S14.2 brief). The view shows what the report holds and computes nothing but each candidate's place in the kit now, so a candidate added since the plan ran shows as added with no new run (.spec-md §10.4). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, in the Plan step's group: `planCandidateList` (`"PlanCandidateList"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `planCandidateRow (candidate : PlanCandidate)` and `addPlanCandidateButton (candidate : PlanCandidate)` are `PlanCandidate_` and `AddPlanCandidate_` followed by `<the plate item's GUID>_<t or r>_<the wavelength in nm, one decimal, invariant culture>`, one private helper writing that key. (2) `PlanView.fs` (step 490): after the report's instrument lines, `Next experiments, in the order the plan adds them:` and a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `planCandidateList`: per ranked step, in order, a row carrying `planCandidateRow` reading `<k>. <the candidate's caption> — rank <r>`, then under `DeterminantPlanCriterion` `, log det <the information's logDeterminant, three decimals>` and under `TargetTracePlanCriterion` `, Σσ² <traceOpt, G4>` when it has one, then `; σ: <each bound as name value, G3, joined by ", ">` when its bounds exist; and, at its end, while writes are offered (`model.kitWrites`, step 185) and its `coverageIn model.kitSetups model.experimentCollection.experiments` (step 482) is `CandidateNotInKit`, `Add to kit` (`addPlanCandidateButton`, an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground`, sending `AddPlannedExperiment candidate`, step 489), or, when it is `CandidateInKit name`, the text `In the kit as <name>.`; before them, one line per report `inKit` candidate, `Already in the kit: <its caption>.`; with no ranked step, `No candidate is open: every candidate is in the kit, or the kit has no Mueller polarimeter or placed plate.`. Tests, in `PlanViewTests` (step 490), over `planKitIn` with a plan run through the posting host: without a trait, `the Plan step ranks the candidates and offers Add to kit for each the kit does not hold`: `planCandidateList` holds QZ-Z's two candidates' `planCandidateRow`s, the first reading `1. QZ-Z (z-cut plate), ` and `rank`, each with its `addPlanCandidateButton`, and over the kit opened read-only no `addPlanCandidateButton`; `the plan view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `PlanCandidateList` and the two derived ids of a test-local candidate. With trait `ui-smoke`: `pressing Add to kit records a planned experiment of the candidate in the kit`: pressing the transmitted candidate's `addPlanCandidateButton` leaves the kit's folder holding one more `.setup-json` and one `.experiment-json` whose role is `PlannedRun`, and that row then reading `In the kit as ` with no `addPlanCandidateButton`. `ScrollExtentTests`' `the kit window's Plan step leaves everything reachable` (step 490) now reaches the candidate rows too. `KitWindowTests`' `a read-only window withholds every write control` finds no `addPlanCandidateButton` over the read-only model.

**Acceptance.** After the candidates show, `planView` MUST list the report's ranked candidates in order with their rank, criterion measure and bounds, offer Add to kit for each the kit does not hold while writes are offered, and show an added one as in the kit; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing Add to kit records a planned experiment of the candidate in the kit`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the Plan step ranks the candidates and offers Add to kit for each the kit does not hold`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the plan view UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the kit window's Plan step leaves everything reachable` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s46 invariants MUST pass.
